    <dcterms:title>An Old-Fashioned Girl</dcterms:title>
    <dcterms:description>Wikipedia page about this book: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/An_Old-Fashioned_Girl</dcterms:description>
    <pgterms:marc508>Produced by David Reed, and David Widger</pgterms:marc508>
    <pgterms:marc520>"An Old-Fashioned Girl" by Louisa May Alcott is a novel first published in 1869. The story follows Polly Milton, a simple country girl who visits her wealthy friend Fanny Shaw's sophisticated Boston family. Overwhelmed by their fashionable lifestyle and troubled by their lack of affection, Polly's warmth and old-fashioned values gradually transform the Shaw household. Years later, Polly returns as a music teacher, navigating friendship, romance, and the family's financial troubles while staying true to her principles. (This is an automatically generated summary.)</pgterms:marc520>
    <pgterms:marc908>Reading ease score: 75.2 (7th grade). Fairly easy to read.</pgterms:marc908>
